       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/mv647hz9361.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "stamped, upright in the upper panel, the whole impression heavily over-inked. Five positions: the first is a solid blob I cannot resolve, the other four are 8, 5, 2, 5, the 5s with their top flag and bowl and the 2 with its base stroke. Five figures read as day, month, year in the way reading.md describes for 14114, so ?8.5.25: the month and year are May 1925, the day is 8, 18 or 28 and the leading figure is not legible. Only the month is entered. Crop 3 carries a pencilled 5669 and crop 4 the printed label, WELTE-MIGNON No. 5669, 'Sergeant Percy', One-step, Richard Fall, played by Sidny Black; crop 2 is blank."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
